{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:24:21.606257Z","id":"aeadde31284bfc47734e5912dd833f64902bb13aaf87802dc92d7286af1507ea","body":{"detail":"A Latin-1 page served as plain `text/html` with `<meta charset=\"iso-8859-1\">` gets U+FFFD for its non-ASCII bytes. Browsers prescan the first 1,024 bytes for a meta charset (WHATWG encoding sniffing). The fetch path (RestSource and BindingSource) decides whether to add that prescan before calling decode, or to pass the sniffed label in as the content type.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":28},"end":{"line":39},"content_hash":"290a5b1e00ccb3f1ee476b09fbe41fe0532dcf15ce0da46b222025a4fb92670c"},"suggested_fix":"Prescan the first 1,024 bytes of an HTML body for <meta charset> or http-equiv Content-Type when content_type names no charset, and use encoding_rs::Encoding::for_label on what it finds.","summary":"decode honours only the Content-Type charset; an HTML page that declares its charset only in <meta charset> decodes as UTF-8","tags":["review","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:24:21.606338Z","id":"12e90a10404f0188cae22ee7c26ba46f4e0055c9299bf2d9ffad8eee83ea3e7c","body":{"detail":"The Worker cannot reach a private network, so this matters for the daemon: its DNS check is is_local_addr (crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs), and a daemon on a carrier-grade NAT or a lab network may reach hosts in 100.64.0.0/10 or 198.18.0.0/15. Spec §5.3 lists private, loopback, link-local and unique-local only.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":164},"end":{"line":171},"content_hash":"0e99a97fb1ee29a080574c48e8a780c478ec9ad9ea5f51117291e7dd3c9f0a5a"},"suggested_fix":"Add 100.64.0.0/10, 198.18.0.0/15, 224.0.0.0/4 and 240.0.0.0/4 (and IPv6 multicast ff00::/8) to local_v4/local_v6 if the owner agrees they are in scope.","summary":"local_v4 refuses only the ranges spec §5.3 names; shared (100.64.0.0/10), benchmarking (198.18.0.0/15), multicast and reserved (240.0.0.0/4) addresses pass","tags":["review","status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:34:46.890590Z","id":"8ee60e5462ca621a60a6e2a865ef93e24b287e0b5923cec74faef482583bcd32","body":{"detail":"The owner's ruling (recorded here because it settles this thread): is_local_addr (crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs) refuses everything that is not public unicast. IPv4: 0/8, 10/8, 100.64/10, 127/8, 169.254/16, 172.16/12, 192.0.0/24, 192.0.2/24, 192.168/16, 198.18/15, 198.51.100/24, 203.0.113/24, 224/4, and 240/4 (which includes 255.255.255.255). IPv6: everything outside 2000::/3 except the forms that embed IPv4, plus 2001::/23, 2001:db8::/32 and 3fff::/20. Mapped, compatible, NAT64 64:ff9b::/96 and 6to4 2002::/16 addresses are judged by their embedded IPv4 address; the rest of 64:ff9b::/16 is refused.","kind":"comment","references":"12e90a10404f0188cae22ee7c26ba46f4e0055c9299bf2d9ffad8eee83ea3e7c","summary":"Ruled: refuse every non-public address, beyond the ranges spec §5.3 lists","tags":["status:decided","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:34:46.891009Z","id":"aa0d29e9189355d261dcd2299523cc2c65fb2f738375fe200e42553a412df95e","body":{"kind":"resolve","summary":"Fixed: the ranges are refused; web::url::tests::every_non_public_address_is_refused passes (bazelisk test //crates/clax-bot:clax_bot_lib_test: 46 passed, 0 failed)","supersedes":"12e90a10404f0188cae22ee7c26ba46f4e0055c9299bf2d9ffad8eee83ea3e7c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/page.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:34:47.102454Z","id":"471838ec7bebe3e9e2dbcb344245ad11b5762c5e56d405671904ddbdaaf7b845","body":{"detail":"A URL in a fenced code block, or after a ]( that no [ opens, counts as a link of the page. Each such link is still text the fetched page holds, so it widens the run's fetchable set (spec §5.2) only by URLs the page itself contains. It can also miss links: an unclosed ]( is read to the next whitespace and not looked at again, which keeps the scan linear (web::page::tests::hostile_pages_are_scanned_in_one_pass).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":179},"end":{"line":306},"content_hash":"1ee57059f6fbae9952f9aeb0fa18542ebb2396d35130d196d71289405050215b"},"suggested_fix":"If extra or missed links matter, replace the scanner with a CommonMark parser that builds for wasm32 (pulldown-cmark, for example) and collect its Link and Image events.","summary":"links_of_markdown is a scanner, not a CommonMark parser: it reads code spans and code blocks as text, and takes the target of any stray ](x","tags":["review","session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot/src/web/url.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-03T04:38:55.439990Z","id":"033b2bb697c55dadcec7ab8d5cd93a8f68d0cd148fe6915b4a4380650358abb8","body":{"kind":"comment","ref":"git:35ae33acf","references":"aa0d29e9189355d261dcd2299523cc2c65fb2f738375fe200e42553a412df95e","summary":"The fix is commit 35ae33acf: is_local_addr's ranges and web::url::tests::every_non_public_address_is_refused","tags":["session:claude-code:ad4c0f0d-1745-4445-8c27-3925ac4b061a"]}}
